This crate translates the WGS84 paths of the NGA GEOTRANS 3.10 sources
vendored in ../libmgrs/geotrans3.10. The original files, modification history,
and notices remain there. SOURCE.json records their upstream archive hashes:
https://github.com/hobuinc/mgrs/blob/main/libmgrs/geotrans3.10/SOURCE.json

Translated sources: CoordinateSystems/mgrs/MGRS.cpp,
CoordinateSystems/tranmerc/TransverseMercator.cpp,
CoordinateSystems/utm/UTM.cpp, CoordinateSystems/ups/UPS.cpp,
CoordinateSystems/polarst/PolarStereographic.cpp, and GeotransConstants.h.

Source classification: UNCLASSIFIED.
GeotransConstants.h notice: Copyright BAE Systems Inc. 2019 ALL RIGHTS RESERVED.
Transverse Mercator algorithm: C. Rollins, April 18, 2006; updated to the NGA
Transverse Mercator document in 2014 and WGS84 book coefficients in 2016.

The Rust translation preserves the projection formulas, coefficient values,
operation order, MGRS cell-center convention, truncation epsilon, special
zones, latitude warnings, and the repository's formatting/input fixes.
It does not expose the upstream configurable ellipsoid/projection classes,
which are not part of the public Python MGRS API.

